1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Buying work fairly takes care.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Velstrian Buy helps a public or private buyer run a clear, even process.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Start with the Requirement Builder. A requirement is what you ask suppliers to deliver.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Step by step, and you can start from a template.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Set the weighting, how much each part counts, and the rubric, the scale you score against.

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Your pipeline shows upcoming and current contracts, with the views public buyers must publish.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:14,000
That includes the section 93 pipeline notice and a contract register you can export.

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:26,000
When bids are in, evaluate. Each evaluator sets their own scores.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The headline is a fixed calculation, the same every time, never by artificial intelligence.

10
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Compare bids brings each supplier to one whole life figure per currency. It does not rank for you.

11
00:01:49,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Record the award, with help for the standstill period and the letters.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:11,000
After award, keep the supplier record current. Score it with a scorecard.

13
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Hold regular reviews, kept with the same supplier.

14
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Track what the contract delivers with the Value tracker. Your primary data is stored in the EU.

15
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Write the requirement, score it fairly, award it cleanly, manage the supplier well.

16
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:48,000
That is Velstrian Buy.
